---
description: Core rules for the pi-rust repository
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow @AGENTS.md. In short:

- pi-rust is a Rust port of upstream pi (earendil-works/pi). Keep JSON field names, session files, settings keys, and config paths compatible with upstream.
- After code changes run `cargo fmt --all`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and the tests of the crates you changed. Before a PR run `cargo test --workspace --locked --no-fail-fast`. Fix every warning.
- Tests never use real provider APIs, keys, or network beyond localhost.
- Conventional Commits set the release version. Never edit versions or CHANGELOG.md by hand.
- Ask before adding a dependency, pushing to `main`, or merging.
